# The secret store's entries (ADR 0032), one NAME=value per line. Values stay empty here.
# Fill a copy outside git (secrets.* is gitignored), then: just secrets-load < secrets.env
# Any source that prints NAME=value lines works, e.g. 1Password:
#   op inject -i secrets.env.tpl | just secrets-load
# with secrets.env.tpl holding lines like github-read-token={{ op://vault/item/field }}.
# After the first load, a file with only the names to change is enough.

# The worker's GitHub read token: fine-grained, Contents: read and Issues: read.
github-read-token=
# The push token: Contents and Pull requests read/write. The worker reads it until the
# pusher is its own service (#240).
github-push-token=
# The Claude subscription token (claude setup-token). The worker reads it and passes it to the
# Claude step until the LLM gateway holds it (#238).
claude-oauth-token=
